Why all the incredulity around here? Admittedly, I'm not much of a
source diver, but I don't see anything in the code that would prohibit
this. There don't seem to be any restrictions on the type of food
object produced from polymorphing another food object, with the
exception of self-laid eggs. Also, crocodile corpses become low boots.

Of course, there's a strong chance of generating a golem while doing
this. Meatballs, eggs, tripe rations, and (I think) corpses can become
flesh golems. Tins become iron golems, and food rations become straw
golems, oddly enough.

It seems that you can generate tins of any variety. It took me ~12
zaps, but I was able to make a pile of 100 tins of spinach like this in
wizmode. I'm not saying that this is necessarily the best use for a
wand of polymorph, but it's certainly possible.



